{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4522","id":4733940167,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU59Ms88AAAABGioxxw","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4522","diff_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4522.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4522.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4522","number":4522,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SF-A00-T25: preserve lease audit chronology across generations","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Task: SF-A00-T25\nRefs #476. This is a regression fix to the completed audit tool; no issue is reopened and no live ownership transfer is performed.\n\n## Problem and delivered behavior\n\nClaim sequences restart at zero, so sorting equal-time events by sequence across generations could put a replacement claim before the previous release and report the wrong owner. Malformed structured comments could also crash sorting, while a stale or mismatched release could erase an otherwise valid reconstructed owner.\n\nOrder equal-time comments by their unique GitHub IDs, preserving decimal integer precision. Without IDs, order by sequence only within one generation; retain input order and mark cross-generation ambiguity explicitly. Invalid structured comments stay visible with auditError and complete:false. Replay checks task, issue, owner, generation and monotonic sequence before changing ownership or lock state. Field-history entries remain informational.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Parent `ca3c083b`: the new 14-case regression suite produced 11 failures and 3 passing controls.\n- Local candidate `f51c5203`, tree `60c0d4c7d84c702f40b1c486783be2c850df3afb`: 32/32 new and existing claim/audit tests passed, no skips, Node 24.19.0 / Linux x64.\n- Command: `node scripts/limited.js node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-reporter=tap planning/contracts/tests/audit-history.test.js planning/contracts/tests/claim-race.test.js`.\n- Whitespace checks passed. Hosted core at the published head remains the required static/manifests/build gate; broad browser/native qualification does not apply to this Node planning regression.\n\nThe GitHub connector publication verifies the exact tested tree; connector-assigned commit metadata changes the commit SHA. Full raw histories are exercised through the existing fake GitHub transport. No passing production GitHub race qualification is asserted.\n\n## Integration\n\nIndependent of PR #4521; both build on the existing main implementation. Two files, no dependencies or hot-file edits. Existing throttled-heartbeat gaps are permitted and explained; an incomplete or ambiguous history cannot become a passing ownership record. No authoritative lease or Project field update is asserted by this new branch.","created_at":"2026-10-04T11:23:48Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T11:27:00Z","closed_at":"2026-10-04T11:26:59Z","merged_at":"2026-10-04T11:26:59Z","merge_commit_sha":"69d398b2a0f5b6cff83a3a79655f574a41d527a